cff-version: 1.2.0
title: OMRFlow
message: >-
  If you use OMRFlow in academic work, please cite it using the metadata in
  this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sajid Muhaimin
    family-names: Choudhury
    email: sajid@eee.buet.ac.bd
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Bangladesh
      University of Engineering and Technology
    website: 'https://www.sajid.bd'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sajidbuet/OMRFlow'
url: 'https://github.com/sajidbuet/OMRFlow'
abstract: >-
  Template-driven optical mark recognition for examination processing.
  OMRFlow designs answer-sheet templates, recognises scanned sheets,
  reconciles them against attendance records, scores them against an answer
  key and generates auditable result workbooks, entirely on a local machine.
keywords:
  - optical mark recognition
  - OMR
  - examination
  - assessment
  - education
  - PySide6
